⦿ .spun — the five-fold spin of Arthur Stuart
node C1 · C1 · ⟦Arthur Stuart:C1:faf2ca⟧

WHO   — Arthur Stuart — the mimic
WHAT  — The mimic — a child whose knack is perfect reproduction of any sound or voice, whom Alvin re-Made down to the body itself so that no Finder's cachet could ever match him again and call him property.
WHERE — C1 · Card  Framework inputs: The Tales of Alvin Maker  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0)
WHY   — Because no soul is owned; because a knack given to mimic the whole living world is given to be free in it; because the boy Alvin could not leave behind became the brother he chose, and the proof that Making is the work of love.
HOW   — By the perfect ear and perfect throat that can echo any voice, birdcall, or word exactly — and, through Alvin's hand, by a body remade molecule from molecule so the slave-catchers' token of his flesh would never again ring true.

awareness — what the node knows of itself:
  They kept a lock of his flesh to own him; Alvin remade the flesh, and the lock owned no one — for a free soul cannot be matched to a chain.

